im(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2024e7-8603-5e5a-8b2e-7cb9aa759b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453380} {:answer/id #uuid "83ac7d4b-d4c5-5c92-8589-e7ec5bddcb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453381}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453381} :answer-field/id #uuid "89392c96-2fc2-5a4d-8885-bb32eafcba1e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454440} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79098b74-c172-54b9-82e2-49824d97c9bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453382} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffeb813-fd36-5776-8ba7-23c839dba453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453383}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453382} :answer-field/id #uuid "be118244-9178-534b-8fc7-3f7c4f68e4fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05113400-1012-5e94-b50e-c93f67bd0a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453384} {:answer/id #uuid "75b2fb9a-b3d9-55ad-8209-77f57b32b7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453385} :answer-field/id #uuid "994ca1fa-debf-5f93-b9db-34b6b1ce3215" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a0f098cb-e297-54fe-a435-e8a16d43aa06" :question/math-academy-id "q-139977" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2b28520-430a-5247-a200-fd5f414e5ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454012} {:answer/id #uuid "f8033251-ab93-5bb9-a145-e5e99be3d388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454013}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454012} :answer-field/id #uuid "da3c91e0-c158-561e-ab32-6e72b9ba78b5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "647ee441-bfd6-5c35-84c4-0fc1e7479328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454014} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e66778-9876-5718-a6e2-1e95fc527bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454015}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454014} :answer-field/id #uuid "030534f1-c9cc-5372-9ff2-bdc749c441e3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31d47ce5-4beb-5f68-bae7-0d361ea95c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454016} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dcdf0f-841a-5b0d-aff9-db735d828b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454017} :answer-field/id #uuid "eced16f4-9e93-50d2-bf88-cdda3960f7ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-79349" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is not invertible\n\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\n- **III.** $A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=5$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446312} {:answer/id #uuid "2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446317} {:answer/id #uuid "a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446339} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fd3f74-8d86-59d5-969d-0f73063566e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446345} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a5d0c5-12bc-5492-a130-1c6bfb4dadcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446312} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b91479d-fc9f-5493-8022-99b07638d6b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "007b2eff-be4f-5ff5-af75-29d7ce49d108" :question/math-academy-id "q-141201" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $\\text{rank}(A)=4?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is an invertible matrix because $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is invertible, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$ because $A$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446321} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446329} {:answer/id #uuid "8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446336} {:answer/id #uuid "f63ddbaf-3159-5f89-a08c-517e465848a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446357} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7d54d8-0b88-5b60-9559-438bba9408ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446360}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446329} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a8a987-b1f9-5fda-b11d-202fd35c0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0a0c9232-89fc-57dc-83d9-632995f2a765" :question/math-academy-id "q-34929" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446333} {:answer/id #uuid "8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446334} {:answer/id #uuid "86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446335} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dd8b94-5449-5e15-bbed-68d5ef48c3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446341} {:answer/id #uuid "f453a8ad-b614-59d8-8bdc-cf9373db8c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446355}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446334} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78aa62f-0e43-5933-85ca-b11f30121e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "40fb1ecb-b40f-5f25-b77a-57f70d15c44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141198" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\nSince $A$ is not invertible, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446314} {:answer/id #uuid "76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446332} {:answer/id #uuid "9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446338} {:answer/id #uuid "f550b866-e3d0-5255-9950-2dbd691d15a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446356} {:answer/id #uuid "f97850ab-a157-554f-a1df-1ca38933ab0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446359}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446314} :answer-field/id #uuid "33cd506b-d09b-50d0-b353-d0e67be14e46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66aeec20-f33b-58e9-909c-e866d7b79c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-141196" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0bd5dd-c5f7-5e5d-b21c-bcdb4e2b830b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528560} {:answer/id #uuid "7385e402-bf26-5641-9a0b-660e87ee9d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528567} {:answer/id #uuid "e0746457-062b-51a1-b39b-1801dcc9dd24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528849} {:answer/id #uuid "e15f2509-6136-5ef5-b754-59b129df8ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528852} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fb30e2-e856-5197-b6a2-1b2e5bd62f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528849} :answer-field/id #uuid "255a02e5-2e2c-5989-905e-69f5223274a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "74f4be02-4fe9-5741-a4d1-7268f77a2f5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142472" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $A$ has $4$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, not $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "77230797-e80e-5644-8b1e-9e3722a0b66d" :step/math-academy-id 19991 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125591}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124433 :question/id #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9961" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\det(A) = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible ![](images/dc/dc72aea1969143a926fd637d3360bb42116b27545a748923069f4ae732bd700f.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\det(A) = 0.$* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nSince $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n.$* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550212 :question-generator/id #uuid "c3528424-1166-5f5e-a67b-38fc540dcd76" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124629.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bec134f4-8ac1-5fd3-a994-79031801df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123603} {:answer/id #uuid "e52ece27-d671-527d-aac5-dac055efd06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123604} {:answer/id #uuid "2e01b189-5d9a-582b-a3da-d616b84586a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123605} {:answer/id #uuid "32960b14-b04a-59a2-9224-0b8a82626700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123606} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffd9fe3-d1f5-5a30-b5aa-c6b01c0e6506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123607}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9eda024b-b844-536e-bf1a-f1efd2375bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123602}] :question/id #uuid "f935b331-7ef7-5abb-b2c6-c78c4160f9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-47586" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n> *If $A$ is a $n \\cdot n$ matrix and $det(A) \\ne 0$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n1. $A$ has no inverse\n2. $Null(A)$ has no basis\n3. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06680c4f-a621-5dc3-875e-3896db2af04b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460023} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1cf54f-05d3-5550-8f3d-cdfa3137d5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460023} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3156979-45c5-5d24-80c1-f665fce48ba8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c8b9c9-048e-580b-90b5-0615fcacbfe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460025} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd76941-0308-57d6-9b7b-3ba6c48171e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460026} :answer-field/id #uuid "44325e4a-3b71-5949-9822-a4ed24085c3a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3989b63d-47f8-5757-bb11-6a685f029eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460027} {:answer/id #uuid "16bc9a89-2517-5c10-b196-866970cad27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460028}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460027} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9665add-7abd-5377-b1f0-9d3eafc436be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f4e1182-d195-5cca-bb1a-601ea1f9c921" :question/math-academy-id "q-47599" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$\n- **III.** $A$ has $5$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=7=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d248bbb6-50b4-5d61-a95e-58f318131503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464246} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d37791a-a285-5a2f-af41-bcd2d8afc075" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3957e353-c39b-5011-af11-d2c9b6787af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} {:answer/id #uuid "8a540690-cbd6-5a7b-8e6a-735ce1ef7a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfe4de2-b1c4-55bb-a60d-27c7be7257dc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f6788d6-5506-57b7-9972-0d793d0b67f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464250} {:answer/id #uuid "67197e1a-6b46-5a73-9b9e-21d0f7711026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d8c4a3-f095-50cd-bcf7-92ff6b429b75" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "795129ab-7204-5692-a97c-e32525213e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142475" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $A$ is invertible\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(A)<n$\n- **III.** $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, according to the invertible matrix theorem, \n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)<n.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$*  $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} {:answer/id #uuid "8712eb23-d6cb-5de9-b4b0-12bf3d790d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ef167d-4bc6-5f6b-9cd2-3492c740a0f5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} {:answer/id #uuid "915b008a-1011-5090-8324-7e9001f057b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b7760-7c88-5d50-8e1a-83c437c15443" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "952b73be-fa27-5c33-ac51-fe0f11cb7be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464256} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6398a3-5006-54e1-b7af-c62ec5fc9eea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$\n\nIII. $A$ has $8$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d1fafe-67a4-5304-b42b-0fa34a95eaff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467578} {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df948ff-c1ab-538f-b99e-ed07682677fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} {:answer/id #uuid "49e7f113-867c-5ee0-a738-ba5b88651827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467581}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8c77e6-a0b4-526b-bf8e-a435b7b66ac1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} {:answer/id #uuid "f8184f79-583b-5721-92be-e461d3dc1a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467583}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58f3fca-628f-5dd4-9837-348f91ad595e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c600e13-fdff-5526-82d0-6659ac10dfc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-47587" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0038a274-1fea-5c60-93f2-4e1f0aa3d0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} {:answer/id #uuid "483dc84e-dfea-55fa-a0cb-de1ae000bf1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468245}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2201cc9-18d3-571c-ae72-347981af2222" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb16210a-cfa0-52ec-956b-46bc4659a344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468246} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5591d-8321-5239-af2f-da46eeeba04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0d4571-9f8e-5b3c-8a20-6f5a2b8194b8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38651f09-b1dd-5820-93c3-99e2657a2fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468248} {:answer/id #uuid "3f51e910-74bd-5148-8e34-b3c363679221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249} :answer-field/id #uuid "020dec00-eb40-52fb-acf8-97681452e138" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e25ee2d5-6236-5cb7-ae46-36798fde6f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-79334" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times $\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d5ed8d-7e60-5db5-b7d1-d96bb65185a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474362} {:answer/id #uuid "10b14067-3f7f-5868-8791-43396e0607b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474363} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb207fd4-1ade-5c72-8528-ba143a738870" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0948d764-f192-5b49-80f0-17ce4b9bcefb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474364} {:answer/id #uuid "f2aade65-5d3a-520b-86ea-745a85070e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474365}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474364} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b6ddd3-8ce7-5c7f-874e-23d5563021dc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dc218b-818c-594c-978b-8b69736909ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474366} {:answer/id #uuid "4999264b-817a-578e-85f5-209e47509eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474367}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474367} :answer-field/id #uuid "25ecf0bb-4395-5d51-99bd-1c0a67d30176" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "251cfe7e-474d-59b2-8ccf-101401daf068" :question/math-academy-id "q-139978" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero\n\nIII. $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $det(A)=0,$ the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero.* $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn,  means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis so the dimension must be greater than zero.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\ne 5,$ which means that $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446323} {:answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} {:answer/id #uuid "65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446326} {:answer/id #uuid "720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446330} {:answer/id #uuid "f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141215" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446343} {:answer/id #uuid "d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446348} {:answer/id #uuid "db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446350} {:answer/id #uuid "f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446354}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" :question/math-academy-id "q-142479" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $A$ is invertible.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$  then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ which means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ actually has a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible it must be $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446313} {:answer/id #uuid "2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446315} {:answer/id #uuid "41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446319} {:answer/id #uuid "662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446327} {:answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141341" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $det(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then we must have $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$ * $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d885553-3afc-5696-a382-4c860965f60c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf00a72-f79f-582d-9aaa-38874ff20b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528592} {:answer/id #uuid "7df12baa-7b1b-58dc-8f63-3871724e61dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528598} {:answer/id #uuid "c974d506-c2bc-