se:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n},$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "7ebf299f-89ad-55ae-8fe6-d0af3bc56dfd" :step/math-academy-id 37508} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124434 :question/id #uuid "fff1daf8-5a1f-54c9-90d7-87710ca00d23" :question/math-academy-id "e-9962" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e58a5f09c9060932ee854feeec0733dc9432c2de658308e3ebdccdd0ef89e5f.svg)\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. What should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/21/21455a41af5743da6f9f4de5e267c17c6037b929a01ba894cfd91530dbb39986.svg)\n\nThe missing expression is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048181} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050028} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050656} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050996}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543842 :question-generator/id #uuid "7536342b-2c7e-5e32-b217-d8346df84acb" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124630.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8cade90-de90-5cc5-a96f-4b62957e1afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :d