nt :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426037} {:answer/id #uuid "562361ed-d031-5fb2-9175-4571a3994648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426047} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7285e7-4a5d-5073-aa0f-ffd3853ddc65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "lI only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426054} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426064} :answer-field/id #uuid "fec9750c-eaeb-571d-b465-6fa1ab05e88d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9fbccd10-1c43-51a4-ad8b-36063e11427d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$  is  invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2024e7-8603-5e5a-8b2e-7cb9aa759b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453380} {:answer/id #uuid "83ac7d4b-d4c5-5c92-8589-e7ec5bddcb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453381}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453381} :answer-field/id #uuid "89392c96-2fc2-5a4d-8885-bb32eafcba1e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454440} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79098b74-c172-54b9-82e2-49824d97c9bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453382} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffeb813-fd36-5776-8ba7-23c839dba453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453383}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453382} :answer-field/id #uuid "be118244-9178-534b-8fc7-3f7c4f68e4fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05113400-1012-5e94-b50e-c93f67bd0a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453384} {:answer/id #uuid "75b2fb9a-b3d9-55ad-8209-77f57b32b7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453385} :answer-field/id #uuid "994ca1fa-debf-5f93-b9db-34b6b1ce3215" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a0f098cb-e297-54fe-a435-e8a16d43aa06" :question/math-academy-id "q-139977" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2b28520-430a-5247-a200-fd5f414e5ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454012} {:answer/id #uuid "f8033251-ab93-5bb9-a145-e5e99be3d388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454013}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454012} :answer-field/id #uuid "da3c91e0-c158-561e-ab32-6e72b9ba78b5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "647ee441-bfd6-5c35-84c4-0fc1e7479328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454014} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e66778-9876-5718-a6e2-1e95fc527bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454015}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454014} :answer-field/id #uuid "030534f1-c9cc-5372-9ff2-bdc749c441e3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31d47ce5-4beb-5f68-bae7-0d361ea95c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454016} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dcdf0f-841a-5b0d-aff9-db735d828b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454017} :answer-field/id #uuid "eced16f4-9e93-50d2-bf88-cdda3960f7ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-79349" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is not invertible\n\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\n- **III.** $A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=5$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446312} {:answer/id #uuid "2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446317} {:answer/id #uuid "a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446339} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fd3f74-8d86-59d5-969d-0f73063566e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446345} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a5d0c5-12bc-5492-a130-1c6bfb4dadcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446312} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b91479d-fc9f-5493-8022-99b07638d6b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "007b2eff-be4f-5ff5-af75-29d7ce49d108" :question/math-academy-id "q-141201" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $\\text{rank}(A)=4?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is an invertible matrix because $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is invertible, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$ because $A$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446321} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446329} {:answer/id #uuid "8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446336} {:answer/id #uuid "f63ddbaf-3159-5f89-a08c-517e465848a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446357} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7d54d8-0b88-5b60-9559-438bba9408ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446360}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446329} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a8a987-b1f9-5fda-b11d-202fd35c0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0a0c9232-89fc-57dc-83d9-632995f2a765" :question/math-academy-id "q-34929" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446333} {:answer/id #uuid "8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446334} {:answer/id #uuid "86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446335} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dd8b94-5449-5e15-bbed-68d5ef48c3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446341} {:answer/id #uuid "f453a8ad-b614-59d8-8bdc-cf9373db8c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446355}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446334} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78aa62f-0e43-5933-85ca-b11f30121e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "40fb1ecb-b40f-5f25-b77a-57f70d15c44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141198" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\nSince $A$ is not invertible, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446314} {:answer/id #uuid "76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446332} {:answer/id #uuid "9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446338} {:answer/id #uuid "f550b866-e3d0-5255-9950-2dbd691d15a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446356} {:answer/id #uuid "f97850ab-a157-554f-a1df-1ca38933ab0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446359}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446314} :answer-field/id #uuid "33cd506b-d09b-50d0-b353-d0e67be14e46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66aeec20-f33b-58e9-909c-e866d7b79c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-141196" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0bd5dd-c5f7-5e5d-b21c-bcdb4e2b830b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528560} {:answer/id #uuid "7385e402-bf26-5641-9a0b-660e87ee9d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528567} {:answer/id #uuid "e0746457-062b-51a1-b39b-1801dcc9dd24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528849} {:answer/id #uuid "e15f2509-6136-5ef5-b754-59b129df8ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528852} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fb30e2-e856-5197-b6a2-1b2e5bd62f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528849} :answer-field/id #uuid "255a02e5-2e2c-5989-905e-69f5223274a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "74f4be02-4fe9-5741-a4d1-7268f77a2f5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142472" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $A$ has $4$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, not $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124433 :question/id #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9961" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\det(A) = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible ![](images/dc/dc72aea1969143a926fd637d3360bb42116b27545a748923069f4ae732bd700f.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\det(A) = 0.$* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nSince $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n.$* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550212 :question-generator/id #uuid "c3528424-1166-5f5e-a67b-38fc540dcd76" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124629.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bec134f4-8ac1-5fd3-a994-79031801df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123603} {:answer/id #uuid "e52ece27-d671-527d-aac5-dac055efd06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123604} {:answer/id #uuid "2e01b189-5d9a-582b-a3da-d616b84586a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123605} {:answer/id #uuid "32960b14-b04a-59a2-9224-0b8a82626700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123606} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffd9fe3-d1f5-5a30-b5aa-c6b01c0e6506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123607}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9eda024b-b844-536e-bf1a-f1efd2375bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123602}] :question/id #uuid "f935b331-7ef7-5abb-b2c6-c78c4160f9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-47586" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n> *If $A$ is a $n \\cdot n$ matrix and $det(A) \\ne 0$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n1. $A$ has no inverse\n2. $Null(A)$ has no basis\n3. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06680c4f-a621-5dc3-875e-3896db2af04b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460023} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1cf54f-05d3-5550-8f3d-cdfa3137d5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460023} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3156979-45c5-5d24-80c1-f665fce48ba8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c8b9c9-048e-580b-90b5-0615fcacbfe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460025} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd76941-0308-57d6-9b7b-3ba6c48171e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460026} :answer-field/id #uuid "44325e4a-3b71-5949-9822-a4ed24085c3a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3989b63d-47f8-5757-bb11-6a685f029eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460027} {:answer/id #uuid "16bc9a89-2517-5c10-b196-866970cad27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460028}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460027} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9665add-7abd-5377-b1f0-9d3eafc436be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f4e1182-d195-5cca-bb1a-601ea1f9c921" :question/math-academy-id "q-47599" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$\n- **III.** $A$ has $5$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=7=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d248bbb6-50b4-5d61-a95e-58f318131503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464246} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d37