 \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, according to the invertible matrix theorem, \n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)<n.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$*  $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} {:answer/id #uuid "8712eb23-d6cb-5de9-b4b0-12bf3d790d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ef167d-4bc6-5f6b-9cd2-3492c740a0f5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} {:answer/id #uuid "915b008a-1011-5090-8324-7e9001f057b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b7760-7c88-5d50-8e1a-83c437c15443" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "952b73be-fa27-5c33-ac51-fe0f11cb7be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464256} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6398a3-5006-54e1-b7af-c62ec5fc9eea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$\n\nIII. $A$ has $8$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d1fafe-67a4-5304-b42b-0fa34a95eaff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467578} {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df948ff-c1ab-538f-b99e-ed07682677fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} {:answer/id #uuid "49e7f113-867c-5ee0-a738-ba5b88651827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467581}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8c77e6-a0b4-526b-bf8e-a435b7b66ac1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} {:answer/id #uuid "f8184f79-583b-5721-92be-e461d3dc1a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467583}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58f3fca-628f-5dd4-9837-348f91ad595e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c600e13-fdff-5526-82d0-6659ac10dfc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-47587" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0038a274-1fea-5c60-93f2-4e1f0aa3d0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} {:answer/id #uuid "483dc84e-dfea-55fa-a0cb-de1ae000bf1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468245}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2201cc9-18d3-571c-ae72-347981af2222" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb16210a-cfa0-52ec-956b-46bc4659a344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468246} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5591d-8321-5239-af2f-da46eeeba04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0d4571-9f8e-5b3c-8a20-6f5a2b8194b8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38651f09-b1dd-5820-93c3-99e2657a2fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468248} {:answer/id #uuid "3f51e910-74bd-5148-8e34-b3c363679221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249} :answer-field/id #uuid "020dec00-eb40-52fb-acf8-97681452e138" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e25ee2d5-6236-5cb7-ae46-36798fde6f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-79334" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times $\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d5ed8d-7e60-5db5-b7d1-d96bb65185a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474362} {:answer/id #uuid "10b14067-3f7f-5868-8791-43396e0607b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474363} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb207fd4-1ade-5c72-8528-ba143a738870" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0948d764-f192-5b49-80f0-17ce4b9bcefb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474364} {:answer/id #uuid "f2aade65-5d3a-520b-86ea-745a85070e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474365}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474364} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b6ddd3-8ce7-5c7f-874e-23d5563021dc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dc218b-818c-594c-978b-8b69736909ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474366} {:answer/id #uuid "4999264b-817a-578e-85f5-209e47509eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474367}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474367} :answer-field/id #uuid "25ecf0bb-4395-5d51-99bd-1c0a67d30176" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "251cfe7e-474d-59b2-8ccf-101401daf068" :question/math-academy-id "q-139978" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero\n\nIII. $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $det(A)=0,$ the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero.* $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn,  means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis so the dimension must be greater than zero.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\ne 5,$ which means that $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446323} {:answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} {:answer/id #uuid "65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446326} {:answer/id #uuid "720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446330} {:answer/id #uuid "f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141215" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446343} {:answer/id #uuid "d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446348} {:answer/id #uuid "db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446350} {:answer/id #uuid "f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446354}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" :question/math-academy-id "q-142479" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $A$ is invertible.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$  then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ which means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ actually has a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible it must be $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446313} {:answer/id #uuid "2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446315} {:answer/id #uuid "41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446319} {:answer/id #uuid "662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446327} {:answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141341" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $det(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then we must have $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$ * $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d885553-3afc-5696-a382-4c860965f60c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf00a72-f79f-582d-9aaa-38874ff20b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528592} {:answer/id #uuid "7df12baa-7b1b-58dc-8f63-3871724e61dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528598} {:answer/id #uuid "c974d506-c2bc-5e7b-97a4-c51ae5371031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528794} {:answer/id #uuid "e94c076f-c6c7-517d-8c55-d74158a4a6fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528875}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} :answer-field/id #uuid "20580d7d-28aa-5c7c-a048-784d0bfa2d4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f1d7f6a4-6114-5671-a52c-7df48bee5e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-141342" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately. \n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn, means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we must have that $A$ is **not** invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n},$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124434 :question/id #uuid "fff1daf8-5a1f-54c9-90d7-87710ca00d23" :question/math-academy-id "e-9962" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e58a5f09c9060932ee854feeec0733dc9432c2de658308e3ebdccdd0ef89e5f.svg)\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. What should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/21/21455a41af5743da6f9f4de5e267c17c6037b929a01ba894cfd91530dbb39986.svg)\n\nThe missing expression is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048181} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050028} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050656} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050996}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543842 :question-generator/id #uuid "7536342b-2c7e-5e32-b217-d8346df84acb" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124630.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8cade90-de90-5cc5-a96f-4b62957e1afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121332} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1a034d-0611-5f21-a47f-fb41d7d10986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121335} {:answer/id #uuid "72b6d84b-4599-5ae1-87e9-228fcb3fc5f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426052} {:answer/id #uuid "ad86e99c-d63c-534c-8616-6b38f0564843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426060} {:answer/id #uuid "c784e28a-945a-50b9-a3c3-88323f6f5bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426062}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426060} :answer-field/id #uuid "36cf5fde-aae3-5ac2-808d-cd031ad46138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b33961fd-1191-51c9-841c-0bdd04b0318b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140766" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\{0\\}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c71e5e-3beb-5717-bf73-407667998f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{dim(Col}({A}^{-1}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269303} {:answer/id #uuid "291a3d81-20e8-5a5d-9323-1fa083aa0241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}({A}^{-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269639} {:answer/id #uuid "34a7b00d-5dfb-51e1-9be3-ea9d486970d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ